WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.900
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.910
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.910
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.870
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.870
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.870
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.790
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.790
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.920
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.110
My name is Kurata Sana, first year
junior high school student.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.780
My manager and driver, Rei-kun.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.870
Aoki Award winner, Mama.
The squirrel is Maro-chan.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.000
Best friend I met in the bathroom,
Fuka.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.580
Mysterious white bat Babbit.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.960
Wearing shoes is troublesome.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.090
Went through all the hardship with
me in New York, Naozumi-kun.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.300
Our relationship is getting
stronger too.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.930
Hayama Akito,
my best friend I think.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.720
Now he's going out with Fuka.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.020
Ahh, hello.
Is this Matsui Fuka's home?

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.310
I'm Sengoku from Jinbo Junior
High Grade 1 class 1.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:16.940
It's about... Fuka's boyfriend,
Hayama Akito-kun.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.070
Sana-chan, look over here about
the rumor that you two are dating...

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.790
Perhaps They Are All
Best Couples

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.330
Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun,
welcome back!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.040
Long time no see.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.170
You two look very close.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.340
I heard there are rumors saying
you two are going out.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.590
Is this true?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.470
Yes! Yes!

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.470
Hey! Wait a second!
Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.720
Are you saying you two are going out?

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.480
We finally have the proof,

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.600
the two who were always denying
they are going out

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.770
finally start dating in public.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.020
What exactly happened in New York?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.400
What exactly happened in New York?

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.240
Sana is back.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.530
Was it yesterday?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.320
We have no idea.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.570
She didn't contact us.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.830
Could it be...

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.580
They were so relaxed when they
said they're going out.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.660
At that time...

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.210
Our relationship is good, that's
because we're friends.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.800
I didn't say anything,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.630
everyone believed the media
and Ishida-kun.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.590
She totally denied it last time.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.720
But it seems real this time.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.220
We can't settle it curtly.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.350
Because we believed the rumors
last time,

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.400
Sana went to New York.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.690
We'd be careful this time,
we should ask Sana first.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.610
- Yeah.
- You're right.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.320
It's better this way.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.410
Whatever you say.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.120
Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun's play
was a big hit in New York.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.830
They were the hottest people in the American media.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:53.420
Maybe Sana-chan won't talk to
us anymore.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.590
That's not possible, Sana-chan
will always be Sana-chan.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.210
I still want to listen to
Sana-chan's weird songs.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.010
And those weird dances.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:07.970
Fuka, very worried

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.970
Waves are tossing in the ocean.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.480
Thank you for taking care
of our daughter.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.690
I'm Matsui Fuka's mother.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.560
I'm Sengoku.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.650
Sorry to bother you.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.820
Have you seen this magazine?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.700
Fuka showed it to me before.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.910
She was so excited.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.570
What's wrong?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.450
Why are you standing up?

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.200
Why are you turning your
back to us?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.250
- The boy in that picture...
- Why are you looking at people like that?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.170
You mean Hayama-kun?

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.340
Did you know that
he's a problem kid...

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.710
Why are you pushing down
the blind?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.220
...pretending to be a nice kid...

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.260
I heard he was a famous
bad boy in elementary school.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.350
Why are you looking outside?

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.520
Bad?

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.230
Bad?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.730
You're the one who's bad!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.650
Eh? You don't have karate practice?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.610
Its been rescheduled to next week.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:01.440
Really?! Then you can come
shopping with me?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.360
Shopping?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.780
I want to buy a bag
for gymnastics practice.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.780
We have a competition next week.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.240
You seem to be very excited.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.240
Thanks, Akito.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.700
Sorry to have bothered you.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.160
That's okay.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.710
You took so long to look at bags, then ended up buying a shirt, why?

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.500
It's just the mood I'm in.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.170
Geez, shopping with girls is so
much trouble.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.590
Later.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.340
Thanks!

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.220
I'm home.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.310
You're back...

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.770
I came back a little late today.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.770
Fuka.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.150
Eh? Papa, you're back early today.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.860
Come here for a second.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.610
I'll go change my clothes first.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.280
Forget that, come sit down.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.780
What is it?

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.950
Fuka's father is a little harsh

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.700
I hate things that turn out to be like this.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.280
What is it?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.870
Where did you go? This is late.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.580
I went shopping with my friend.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.620
Is that friend of
yours Hayama-kun?

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.290
Was it Hayama-kun?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.630
That's right.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.510
What's your relationship with
Hayama-kun?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.220
You...

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.680
What do you mean?

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.430
Fuka, Papa is worried about you.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.560
Worried about what?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.430
Sengoku-sensei called your mom to school.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:21.860
She heard Hayama-kun was a violent
troublemaker in elementary school.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.110
Sengoku-sensei...?

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.780
Sengoku-sensei is
worried about you too.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:32.200
That's not true, Sengoku-sensei is
not worried about me at all.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:38.540
But, if you... and... Hayama-kun
remain friends...

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.170
Sengoku-sensei will never care
about me!

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.050
He just hates Akito,
he sees him as an enemy!

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.920
But was his violent past true?

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.430
That's...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:53.100
We heard it from a kid who was in
the same school.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.600
He was always causing trouble.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.810
But now he's...

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.980
So he really is a problem kid...

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.980
Teachers won't lie.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:08.030
Fuka, Papa and Mama didn't say you
can't be with him,

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.110
but just keep your
distance from him.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:14.580
If you have time to be in a
magazine like this,

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.540
why didn't you do something useful?

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.790
Like studying... sports...

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.080
Fuka!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.920
Akito is
not that kind of person.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.340
Sengoku-sensei is
the real slimy guy.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.840
Where are you going, Fuka?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.840
I'm going out to cool off.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.100
Fuka!

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.440
This week's Sana-chan.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.230
Uh... this doesn't make sense.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.990
Just a second.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.450
Akito, it's Fuka-chan.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.410
She sounds strange.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.330
She's all yours, good luck.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.080
What happened?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.250
Fuka.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.090
Akito.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.630
What's wrong?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.890
No matter what happened,

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.470
staying out this late is very
dangerous.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.520
I'm sorry,
I just wasn't in a good mood,

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.730
and I wanted to see you.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.900
Did I scare you?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.360
What happened?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.110
It's... actually nothing.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:39.120
I... just wanted to see you...
I'm so weird.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.870
What happened?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.580
Tell me.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.420
It's actually nothing.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:50.960
Tell me.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.720
I had a fight with my parents...

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.390
...about the picture...

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.560
It's nothing serious.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.730
And Sengoku-sensei...

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.440
Sengoku?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.900
He called my mom to school,
he said some bad things about you.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.780
What does he want anyway?

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.120
If he has something to say to us,

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.000
he should just tell us straight to
our faces.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.460
Why did he have to call my mom?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.750
That teacher is so low.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:33.920
Let's just think this is all
Sengoku-sensei's fault, and forget this.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.970
Hey Akito, aren't you mad?

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.890
This is rare,
it was good thing I called you.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.140
You...

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.680
What?

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.310
You're very interesting.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.690
Really?

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.860
Actually, you're very weird.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.530
I just don't want you to be angry.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.980
Thanks.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.990
I always feel safe
when I'm with Akito.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.330
Sometimes it makes me blush.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.080
That's how it is.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.120
That hurts.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.750
But I'm happy,
just to be like this.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.170
I like the Akito standing
in front of me.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.050
Wait here.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.510
What?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.680
Wait a moment.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:18.970
What?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.640
What are you doing?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.350
Listen to it later.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.310
I'll walk you home.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.100
Wait, Akito.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.440
My home is that way.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.690
Don't play with fire.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.280
When can you remember
where my home is?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.530
Ah... you two are so close.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.610
Babbit's Counting Song

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.530
Babbit is
going to sing with gusto!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.200
One, and Two, and One, and Two, Four!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.500
Yolole, Yolole, Yolole-hee.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.500
Yell on top of a mountain.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:52.540
Yolole, Yolole, Yolole-hee.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.500
Yell on top of a mountain.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.130
One, and Two and One, and Two, Five!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.430
I know a day like this will come.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.430
I understand, and goodbye.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.390
I know a day like this will come.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.520
I understand, and goodbye.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.190
One, and Two, and One, and Two, Six!

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.440
Even though there are many unhappy events in life

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.030
Life is not filled only with unhappiness

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.530
The world is not a happy piece. Who's that?

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.360
Even though there are many unhappy events in life

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.030
Life is not filled only with unhappiness

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.530
The world is not a happy piece. Who's that?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.540
Life is good.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.790
Akito's message,

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.670
I wonder what's in it.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:45.100
Akito recorded on the wrong side.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.720
Moron.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:12:00.530
{parte b}

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.450
Weekly magazine Dolabi.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.030
Magazine Class.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:05.820
Nagasaki News.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.450
Monthly magazine Maggie.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:13.170
All the magazines published today
have Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun's picture.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.790
Are these all about them dating?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.250
Maybe they did have relations.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.880
Aya-chan,
what you said is a little...

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.840
This kind of news are so
exaggerated,

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.970
maybe the reporters made it up.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.430
But they could be really going out.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.020
They are really doing it.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.900
When did you
start talking like this?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.320
Sana, why?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.400
Why didn't you tell us?

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.490
I'm sorry, everyone...

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.410
I'm sorry.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.620
Hurry back, Sana.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.450
Hurry back.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.330
After Sana came back to Japan,

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.040
she seems very busy.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.420
Their TV series
is about to start filming.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.260
We won't be able to see
Sana-chan for a while.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:07.180
Then let's go visit her.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.970
Eh? Go to Sana-chan's home?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.890
Let's have a welcome party.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.180
That's a great idea, right?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.770
Since you're the boss,
you can call her.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.020
- Eh? I'm the boss?
- Do your best.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.150
Boss

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.070
Hello? Sagami-san?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.780
It's me, Tsuyoshi-kun.
Long time no see.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.070
I've been great.

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.240
You're earning a lot of money to
yourself.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.780
How was the New York trip?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.500
Really? How was the weather?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.120
Is he an old man?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:41.210
Tsuyoshi is good
at ass kissing

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.330
I forgot to tell you, after school,

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:41.090
going shopping, or going
out, instead of going straight home is bad.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.340
Sana-chan is shooting a commercial
with Naozumi-kun.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.970
Eh? Welcome party?

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.840
That's great, Sana-chan wants to
see all her friends too.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.600
How's Sunday afternoon?

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.470
OK, I'll call you back, bye.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.930
It's Sunday.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:59.190
Let's ask Hisae-chan them to come
with us, they want to see Sana-chan too.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:01.570
Look at this guy from the winner
of best couple.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.110
- He's so cute.
- Which one is he?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.110
He looks so gentle.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.570
He looks so handsome,
and seems very dependable.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.370
Look over there.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:16.160
They are saying you're dependable
and gentle.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.620
- He's blushing.
- You are getting popular.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.960
It's the picture making him look
like he's gentle and dependable.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.960
But it's not true in reality.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:28.510
That's not true, he cares a lot
about me.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.510
Then what did you just say
a minute ago?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.640
Can I tell them that the couple in
the magazine is here?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.430
- No.
- It's OK.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.310
Then I'll tell them.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.350
Hey, over here...

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.820
- I'm going back.
- Hey, Akito...

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.190
Tsuyoshi-kun, are you all right?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.070
He hasn't hit me in a long time,
I was careless.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.360
You're careless
all the time.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.150
Careless?

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.120
It's so embarrassing.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:09.130
What will you say when you see
the picture?

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.260
What's this?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.970
Fuka is too good for Hayama.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.350
You're so ugly...

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.650
Shut up!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.990
Sana...

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.870
Welcome party

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.660
There are so many people.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.160
We haven't seen Sana-chan in
a long time too.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.210
We can help Sana-chan cheer up.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.540
What?!
This is Sana's house?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.630
This is your first time here?

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.300
Hello! Everyone...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.550
Sana.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.170
Long time no see!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.630
Long time no see!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.760
Why are we standing here for,
let's get inside.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.470
OK, excuse me!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.310
Everyone, welcome.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.480
- Welcome.
- My working partner.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:07.440
It's Kamura Naozumi.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.650
There are people I haven't seen
before, I'm Kamura Naozumi.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.070
The legendary couple...

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.410
You're open minded.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.490
They look like a couple no matter
how you look at it.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.330
This is so great. Naozumi-kun came
to this party.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.080
I knew today was Sana-chan's
welcome party,

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.120
and a lot of her friends were
going to come.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.170
I want to join you too.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.000
That's no problem.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.920
We're all friends, right,
Akito-kun?

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.550
- Take a picture with me.
- Me too!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.300
He's really popular.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:38.470
Look, this is me and Naozumi-kun
in the show in New York.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.220
Ah, let me see.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.890
It's so pretty.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:45.270
We were twin fairies.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.190
That's right.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.020
- What's the story about?
- Was it a love story?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.360
Yeah, helping unhappy couples,

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.820
using our magic to give them
a happy ending.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:56.620
We can't fit in.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.280
Being here is enough.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:01.910
But, I haven't seen Sana in
a long time.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.960
I have a lot of things
to say to her.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.040
She's too busy.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:13.010
She's a busy body, a show off,

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:17.050
you'll be dragged around if
you're near her.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.060
Well, that's who she is.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.640
Is she really that kind of person?

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.440
Sana-chan's story in
New York is so funny.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.610
Well, I'm happy to see her full
of energy again.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.990
Welcome.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.530
Ah, long time no see.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:38.030
Recently, Sensei is very
interested in plants.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.660
But this time it's a failure.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.490
Watering is a lot of trouble.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:44.450
So you are Matsui Fuka.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.710
Yes, thank you
for taking care of Sana.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.710
That's what I'm suppose to say.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:53.300
But it's been a long time since
there have been this many people in the house.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.010
Maro-chan is excited too.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:57.130
Please enjoy.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.680
I'll go look at some new plants
I bought.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.680
Drink some wine,
the warmth will protect you.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:03.810
Yes.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:07.020
You should consider her appearance
normal.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.270
Really?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.570
Akito, you know a lot about
Sana's family.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.570
That's because I've known her
since elementary school.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.650
I didn't know that.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.990
Hey, what's the matter,
you look tired.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.240
I'm not done yet,
let me continue...

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.330
- I'm tired.
- We can't beat Sana-chan.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.880
Everyone is sleeping with a grin
on their faces.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.050
It's like afternoon naptime in
kindergarten.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:38.010
But we can finally start talking
with Sana.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.130
Right.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.890
Long time no see.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.010
You're so cold,

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:47.640
went to New York, and you didn't
contact us when you came back.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.770
- I feel guilty too.
- I couldn't sleep.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.900
The decision to go to New York was
very sudden to me too.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.570
And a lot has happened there.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:00.200
But in New York,
the most amazing thing is...

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.030
That's right, let me
show you something.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.240
This, this...

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.120
What's this?

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.160
He looks the same as Akito-kun.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.370
His name is Brad, he was a
troublemaker too.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.380
He caused me a lot of trouble.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:16.050
I can't believe it, there's someone
who looks like Hayama in another country.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.800
But we eventually became friends.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.010
He's simple person.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:24.470
- Naozumi-kun is simple too.
- What are you talking about?

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:26.640
Very simple, but...

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:30.230
Are you going to mention that again?
I told you not to.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:33.520
It's not like that,
innocent like a child...

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.860
You're a kid yourself.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.690
No... it's not like that.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.740
It's a little romantic...
I think too much...

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.610
I'm a very good person.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.120
Excuse me...

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.620
Can I ask you two a question?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:47.830
What is it?

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.250
Eh... don't be angry... um...

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.790
What is it?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:58.130
You two... Sana-chan and
Naozumi-kun...

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.090
How should I say this...

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.550
- Are you two having relations?
- Aya-chan...

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.930
We didn't want to listen to
the media,

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.600
that's why I think we should
ask you first.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.390
Are you two having relations?
Tell us.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.100
Aya-chan, your wording is not
very nice...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:16.520
- We're in a relationship.
- That's right.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.980
It'd be...

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.900
Having a relationship,
I'm not sure what is means.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.700
But we went through a lot
in New York...

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:27.120
Especially me.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.330
That's right.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.330
What happened in New York, it's
too much trouble to explain it to the media.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.710
So I'll just say it here.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:40.050
During the play, my mental state
wasn't stable.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:45.430
At that time, Sana-chan stayed with me all the time. She laughed with me...

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:49.180
cried with me, got angry at me,
cheered me on...

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.430
She helped me a lot.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.560
Sana-chan is very important to me.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:21:02.150
I feel warmth to know he needs me.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:06.320
So that's why, I feel I'm doing
this for myself.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.740
And I feel Naozumi-kun is the most
important thing to me too.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.500
- Right?
- This is the first time I heard you say that.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.540
Ah, you're right, I guess I'm not
good at saying things like this.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:20.500
If you said it earlier, I would
have been even happier.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.300
Then this time is for real.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.260
Then, Tsuyoshi-kun and I,

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.840
Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun,

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.390
Fuka-chan and Hayama-kun,

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.260
are the best matching couples.

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.520
Oh right, I have something here.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:33.890
This.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.100
When did you bring this?

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.350
What? What?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:39.610
Stop it, what's so great about it?

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.900
- Look, this is me and Aya-chan.
- It's really you.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:42.980
What about our picture?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.490
Ah, it's Hayama and Fuka.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.820
Isn't it great?

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:48.780
- Naozumi-kun, here, here.
- It's really them.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.870
You got best couple award.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.910
That's right.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.920
Hayama... I'm happy for you.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:05.510
You two are perfect...

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:09.180
Hayama and Fuka.

